WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.367
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.133
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.834
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.467
I am so excited about this.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.667
Steve Martin and Martin Short
are my guests tonight!

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.334
-Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:19.634
-Backstage, I was like,
"You guys are my comedy heroes."

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:24.100
And they were like, "Oh, my God.
We're such big fans of us, too."

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.467
Well, I'm in
a good mood right now

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:26.934
because we're right in
the middle of

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:29.000
the holiday season right now,
and I love the holiday season.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love it.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.834
By the way, here's a little tip
for anyone buying presents.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.767
Whatever you buy,
just say you got it on Etsy

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.100
so everyone thinks a lot of
thought went into it.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.400
That's what I do.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.934
Of course, gift cards
are always a popular option.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.567
And I like
the Amazon gift cards,

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.267
because they basically say,
"The only thing

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:51.133
I 100% know about you
is that you want a gift."

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.133
Meanwhile, I saw that tomorrow
is National Christmas Card Day.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.200
And I've already seen some

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.667
pretty interesting cards
this year.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.167
I'll show you some of the
ones I've got.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:00.634
For instance, look at this.
This is a card from Aaron Judge.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:01.734
On the front, it says...

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.234
Open it up, and it says...

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.868
You go, "Wait. Come on."

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:14.300
Here's another one I got.
-They're very specific, yeah.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.534
-Here's a card from
"Good Morning America."

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:16.567
It says...

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:19.667
You open it up, it says...

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.834
♪♪
-Wow!

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.667
-I don't know what it means.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:29.234
-Morning.
-Here's a card from Joe Biden.

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.234
It says...

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.367
You open it up, it says...

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.367
Wow.

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:50.767
Here's a nice card
I got from Elon Musk.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:51.834
It says...

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.300
Open it up, it says...

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.334
-Wow!
-That's nice.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.968
Here's a card from
Herschel Walker. It says...

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.300
Open it up, it says...

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:10.801
And you go, "Well, he's trying.
He's trying."

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.467
-Yeah, he's trying.
He falls down, he gets back up.

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.601
-Yeah. And, finally, here's a
card from Vice President Harris.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.601
It says...

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:18.634
Open it up, it says...

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:23.300
Everyone's in the spirit.
Very nice.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.200
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.567
Let's get to some news.
Everybody's talking about this.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.467
Today, 10 months after
she was detained,

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:34.968
Brittney Griner
was freed from Russian custody

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:36.434
in a prisoner exchange...

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:37.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.601
...between The White House
and the Kremlin.

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.033
You could tell Biden
was fired up

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:44.067
when he began his speech with,
"It's Brittney [bleep]

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:47.300
And you go, "Hey."

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.300
Putin is no stranger
to prisoner swaps.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.667
In fact, "Prisoner Swap"

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.234
is the most popular
reality show in Russia.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.667
Yeah, there was a prisoner swap.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.934
In exchange for Griner,
Moscow received

00:02:57.934 --> 00:03:00.100
the notorious Russian
arms dealer

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.033
who was known as
"The Merchant of Death."

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:04.300
-Ooh!
-Can we see what he looks like?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.434
-Ooh!

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:08.734
-When asked for a statement,
he said,

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:11.000
"If your wife has ever said,
'Come move these

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.434
rocket launchers
so I can take a bath,'

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:16.434
you might be
an international arms dealer."

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.634
Hey, I read that the C.E.O.
of Build-A-Bear Workshop

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:26.834
said 40% of their shoppers are
now teenagers and adults.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:27.968
It's little surprising,

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.367
but it does explain
the new ad campaign.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.601
Check this out.

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:33.767
-At Build-A-Bear Workshop,
we're not just for kids.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.501
We're for kids of all ages,

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:37.167
so the next time
you're at the mall,

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:39.334
stop on by and build a bear.

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:40.467
Build a bestie.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:41.534
Build a boss.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:42.868
Build a boyfriend.

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:45.400
Build a better life,
the one you used to dream about

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.767
back when everything
still felt exciting and vital,

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:50.100
because age is nothing
but a number,

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.200
a big, terrible number,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.534
a grandfather clock
about to strike,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.968
the sound of whose
bong, bong, bong

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:00.567
will never be heard by
the lifeless bear

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:03.334
you clutch to as a totem of
what was once possible

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:04.868
but no longer is.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.234
Build-A-Bear Workshop --

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.100
we're going
through something right now.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.901
-Wow!
-That explains it.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:13.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow!

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.100
-Well, guys,
"Avatar: The Way of Water"

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.501
finally comes out next week.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:18.734
A lot of people are
excited for it.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:19.934
It's getting great reviews.

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:22.300
But since it's been
almost exactly 13 years

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.467
since "Avatar" came out,
we thought it'd be helpful

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.400
to recap what happened
in the first movie.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.534
So here now with a rap recap
is Tariq from The Roots.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.667
Take it away, Tariq.
-One, two, three.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.300
-♪ I said, I don't remember ♪

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.334
[ Music stops ]

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:44.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:50.534
-I heard about a man in Florida
who was arrested for

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:51.801
allegedly stealing over

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:55.601
$1,300 worth of
toothbrushes from Walgreens.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.100
Yep, the man was convicted after

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.467
four out of five jurors
found him guilty.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:02.033
Guys, we have
exactly seven shows left

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.901
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.801
that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:08.767
It is time for "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters."

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.067
Here we go.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:12.567
-♪ "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:16.200
♪ Seven days left ♪

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.367
-That's right.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.868
Every show between
now and Christmas,

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.868
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:23.934
a magnificent Christmas sweater

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:26.334
from the
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:27.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:30.300
Since there are
seven shows left,

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.634
let's open door number 7.

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:35.701
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:37.767
Ooh! Here, right?

00:05:37.767 --> 00:05:38.834
Go for it.
Whenever you're ready.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.968
-Ready.
-Yeah, go.

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.767
Oh, wow!

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:45.334
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:49.400
Nice. Thank you very much.
Look at this.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.367
Disco Santa.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.033
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:05.667
Everyone look at
your seat number.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.534
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:09.400
Quest, can I get
a drumroll, please?

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.501
[ Drumroll ]
Who wants a sweater?

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:11.501
This is a goody, this one.

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:14.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:17.834
Here we go!
-Here we go.

00:06:17.834 --> 00:06:19.200
-114!

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.167
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:24.634
Hey, come on.

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:27.133
Come on.

00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:29.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:34.267
Hi!

00:06:35.701 --> 00:06:39.067
Nice to meet you. How are you?
Stand right there.

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:40.634
-Right over here.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.434
-What is your name
and where are you from?

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:44.467
-I'm Jaslene and I'm from
Norwalk, Connecticut.

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:47.334
-Hey! Jaslene, welcome!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.968
Norwalk, it gets very cold
this time of year.

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:52.267
And you have
a beautiful sweater.

00:06:52.267 --> 00:06:53.667
-Thank you.
-You almost can't top that.

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:56.601
But then you have this.

00:06:56.601 --> 00:06:58.200
Do you have anything like
this in your wardrobe?

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.534
-No, it's unique.
-Yes, thank you.

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:02.100
That's a nice way of putting it.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.167
Would you like to try it on
for everyone?

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:04.868
-I would.
-Oh, this is exciting.

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:07.467
There you go. Roots?

00:07:07.467 --> 00:07:09.501
There you go, bud.

00:07:09.501 --> 00:07:11.133
-Oh, we've got to do
the hands first.

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:13.033
-Oh, yeah,
your hands go through.

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.968
Oh, yeah. Oh, no, no, no.
I can already tell.

00:07:14.968 --> 00:07:18.000
This is going to be gorgeous.
-I love it.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.334
-Are you -- Come on.
Look at us. You look great.

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:22.801
Come on. How cute.

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:24.934
Yeah, give it up
for our winner right there.

00:07:24.934 --> 00:07:26.200
Congratulations.
-Thank you!

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.501
-Guys, stick around.

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:30.033
We'll be right back with
Steve Martin and Martin Short.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:31.300
Come on back.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

